# Dagric OS Pro — Creator suite
# (These lists are removed for free-edition builds; the free ISO stays lean.)

# Second browser: open-source Chromium alongside Firefox ESR
chromium

# Email, calendar, contacts
thunderbird

# Thunderbird's interface in the five languages Dagric ships, for the same
# reason Firefox and LibreOffice get theirs in apps.list.chroot: the desktop
# around it is already translated, so leaving this one English makes the
# machine look half-finished rather than lean. Verified absent from the Aug-4
# Pro ISO — /usr/lib/thunderbird had no extensions or distribution locale dir.
# Spanish is es-es here, not es; there is no thunderbird-l10n-es. Confirmed
# with `apt-get install -s`. 3.2 MB for all five.
thunderbird-l10n-de
thunderbird-l10n-es-es
thunderbird-l10n-fr
thunderbird-l10n-it
thunderbird-l10n-pt-br

# The FULL office suite (free edition ships Writer/Calc/Impress only)
libreoffice
# LibreOffice Base needs a JVM and will not open one without it. The suite is
# pinned above as "the FULL office suite", and Base is the half of it that
# depends on java: `libreoffice-base Recommends: default-jre | java-runtime`,
# which --apt-recommends false drops. Verified absent from the built image —
# out/manifest/pro.packages has no default-jre and no java of any kind.
# A Pro owner opens the database application the paid tier sold them and gets
# "LibreOffice requires a Java runtime environment (JRE) to perform this task".
# -headless, not the full default-jre: Base needs the runtime, not a second
# desktop Java with its own icons and browser plugin.
default-jre-headless

# The JRE above lets Base OPEN. It does not make the wizards work. The four
# "Use Wizard to Create Table / Query / Form / Report" buttons on Base's start
# page are Java, and their .jar files live here — without them the buttons do
# nothing at all, silently, which is worse than the missing-JVM dialog that was
# fixed by adding the runtime. 625 KB.
libreoffice-java-common

# Creative tools
inkscape
# Inkscape's Extensions menu is Python and its libraries are Recommends only.
# Without scour, File -> Save As -> Optimized SVG raises a Python traceback
# naming a missing module instead of saving. python3-lxml and python3-numpy
# back most of the Generate/Modify Path entries.
python3-scour
python3-lxml
python3-numpy
gimp
blender
krita

# Krita's interface in the five languages Dagric ships. Same reasoning as the
# Firefox, LibreOffice and Thunderbird langpacks: on a fully translated desktop
# a single entirely-English creative application reads as half-finished rather
# than lean, and Krita is the one a Pro buyer opens first. 24 MB, and it is the
# largest single thing added here — it carries every language Krita has, because
# Debian ships no per-language split for it.
krita-l10n

# Video: recording and editing
obs-studio
kdenlive
# frei0r-plugins is where most of kdenlive's effects actually live — colour
# grading, blur, distortion, keying and several standard transitions. It is a
# Recommends of kdenlive and was dropped, so the Effects panel on the shipped
# Pro image is missing most of its entries with no error to explain why. The
# video editor is one of the tier's headline applications.
frei0r-plugins

# Backup: local + any cloud (Borg with a friendly GUI, rclone for
# Drive/Dropbox/S3/OneDrive and 70+ other providers)
borgbackup
vorta
rclone
# Google Drive mounted natively in Dolphin (KDE-native, complements rclone's
# CLI with a browse-in-the-file-manager experience).
kio-gdrive
# kio-gdrive alone cannot SIGN IN: the Google entry in Online Accounts lives in
# kaccounts-providers, which is only a Recommends and so is dropped by our
# no-recommends policy — leaving the advertised "Google Drive in Dolphin" with
# no way to add an account. The OAuth login window needs the QtWebEngine QML
# module. (Audit: verified missing in the shipped Pro image.)
kaccounts-providers
# signon-ui-qt renders the sign-in window and signon-ui-service is the D-Bus
# service behind it. NOT "signon-ui" — that name does not exist in trixie and
# would have aborted the Pro chroot stage an hour into the build. The real
# names are in kaccounts-integration's own Recommends line, which is where a
# package name should always be read from rather than guessed:
#   Recommends: kaccounts-providers, signon-ui-qt, signon-ui-service, systemsettings
# Without them Online Accounts cannot
# complete a single login. kaccounts-providers is here and correct; signond is
# pulled in; but the UI plugin that draws the Google consent screen is a
# Recommends and was dropped. Verified: out/manifest/pro.packages has
# kaccounts-integration and kaccounts-providers, and no signon-ui.
# The owner picks System Settings -> Online Accounts -> Google, signond opens an
# authentication session with nothing to display it, and the dialog either never
# appears or closes immediately. The advertised Google Drive integration in
# Dolphin can therefore never be set up.
signon-ui-qt
signon-ui-service
qml6-module-qtwebengine

# Optional scheduled-snapshot GUI. The automatic pre-update rollback stack
# is snapper + grub-btrfs (configured at first boot on the default btrfs
# install); Timeshift adds user-scheduled restore points on top, and its
# rsync mode covers manual ext4 installs that snapper's btrfs flow can't.
timeshift

# Mobile integration — notifications, file transfer, remote input,
# clipboard sync with Android/iOS via the KDE Connect app
kdeconnect

# A more colorful, modern icon set for the Pro look
papirus-icon-theme

# Full international text — CJK + broad Unicode so nothing renders as tofu
# boxes. Kept in Pro so the free edition stays lean; free users can add
# languages on demand through Discover.
#
# THE SIZE WAS WRONG BY MORE THAN DOUBLE. This comment said ~200 MB, and so
# did docs/TEST-REPORT.md and, once it was copied onto the Pro sales page, a
# page a customer reads before paying. Debian publishes the real figures for
# trixie/fonts-noto-cjk: 54 MB download, 89 MB installed. Nothing else Pro
# adds closes that gap — the only other Pro-only font packages are
# fonts-dejavu, fonts-dejavu-extra and libfontconfig1:i386, none of them
# large. Overstating a paid asset by 2x on the page that asks for the money
# is the kind of number that makes a reader doubt the rest of it.
fonts-noto-cjk

# And TYPING Chinese, not only reading it. Free ships the fcitx5 input-method
# stack with Korean and Japanese engines — the full reasoning lives with the
# block in desktop.list.chroot. Chinese lands here because its cost is
# different in kind: fcitx5-chinese-addons drags the libime language models,
# and it belongs beside the font that makes its output render. Same split,
# same reasoning, same edition as fonts-noto-cjk directly above.
fcitx5-chinese-addons

# System maintenance GUI: clean caches, logs, and freed disk space visually
bleachbit

# GTK virtual filesystem — network locations and MTP phones inside the GTK
# apps Pro ships (GIMP, Inkscape file dialogs)
gvfs-backends

# ── Curated open-source additions (all DFSG-free, Debian main) ──
# Privacy & ownership — passwords in a local vault (keepassxc), direct
# device-to-device sync with no cloud (syncthing), and per-app Flatpak
# permission control (flatseal).
keepassxc
syncthing
flatseal
# Creative depth beyond the core suite: RAW photo development (darktable),
# multitrack audio (audacity — Debian build ships no telemetry), and video
# conversion (handbrake).
darktable
audacity
handbrake
# Everyday utility done the open way: an ad-free torrent client and a visual
# disk-usage explorer.
qbittorrent
filelight

# OBS WITH NO PLUGINS IS THE PAID EDITION'S FIRST DISAPPOINTMENT. site/pro.html
# sells OBS Studio by name — "record and stream with the same tool the pros
# use" — and it is one of six headline apps. Week one the buyer opens it, clicks
# + to add a source, and finds the stock set only. The browser source, the
# scene-switching and the filters that every tutorial they will watch assumes
# are in obs-plugins, which apt does not take because Dagric builds with
# --apt-recommends false.
#
# 3 MB on a 3.8 GB image, and the difference between the application the site
# promised and a stripped one.
obs-plugins
